== 1.9 Chapter 1 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The unit of heredity that carries information from parent to offspring is the],
  [gene],
  [chromosome],
  [nucleolus],
  [centromere]
)

#mcq(2, [A human body cell contains how many chromosomes?],
  [92],
  [22],
  [46],
  [23]
)

#mcq(3, [A gamete is described as haploid because it contains],
  [one set of chromosomes],
  [two sets of chromosomes],
  [no chromosomes],
  [only sex chromosomes]
)

#mcq(4, [The number of chromosomes in a human sperm cell is],
  [46],
  [23],
  [92],
  [44]
)

#mcq(5, [Chromosomes that carry the same genes in the same order are said to be],
  [mutant],
  [haploid],
  [analogous],
  [homologous]
)

#mcq(6, [The point at which two chromatids of a chromosome are joined is the],
  [telomere],
  [centromere],
  [chromomere],
  [centriole]
)

#mcq(7, [The molecule that carries the genetic code is],
  [deoxyribonucleic acid],
  [protein],
  [starch],
  [lipid]
)

#mcq(8, [The four bases found in DNA are],
  [guanine, thymine, uracil and adenine],
  [adenine, guanine, cytosine and uracil],
  [adenine, thymine, uracil and cytosine],
  [adenine, guanine, cytosine and thymine]
)

#mcq(9, [In DNA, adenine always pairs with],
  [cytosine],
  [guanine],
  [uracil],
  [thymine]
)

#mcq(10, [A sequence of three bases on DNA that codes for one amino acid is a],
  [codon],
  [anticodon],
  [chromomere],
  [centromere]
)

